}

// An aggregator over leaf children that exposes the same
// underlying state through three modes:
//   - bulk:       total sum across all children (aggregate)
//   - harmonic:   count of children (per-class projection;
//                 for homogeneous accept, this is just the
//                 cardinality)
//   - resolution: largest single child value (tail / edge)
//
// All three read self.children, the locus's typed collection
// of accepted coordinatees. They share the locus's arena (per
// design commitment F.5), so no copy or extra allocation
// happens between modes.

locus LeafL {

//
// m32 shipped defaults on free fns; m34 extended them to locus
// `fn` methods called via `self.method(...)`. Modes
// (`bulk` / `harmonic` / `resolution`) had been left out at
// codegen-declare time with a "not yet lowered" rejection. The
// CHECKPOINT polish entry blamed F.10 for a "tighter param
// surface", but F.10 only governs mode-keyword-as-member-name
// parsing — not param shape. Modes ARE just locus methods named
// after their kind, and `lower_self_method_call` already routes
// Fn and Mode through the same default-fill-in path. The only
// thing m54 changes is lifting the codegen-declare rejection
// (replaced with the same suffix-only ordering check the locus
// `fn` path already uses).
//

//   - bulk:       arithmetic mean of every child's
//                 extrapolation at t_target (the consensus
//                 estimate; all sources weighted equally)
//   - harmonic:   spread = max - min across children (how
//                 much do the sources disagree at t_target)
//   - resolution: the single child whose extrapolation is
//                 closest to the bulk mean (most-central
//                 source; least-outlier; the source the
//                 cluster agrees with most)
//
// This is the heart of the triangulator app: each multicast
// feed becomes a LeadingEdge child; the bulk/harmonic/
// resolution triple is the lotus-first projection surface
// downstream consumers query.

        return out;
    }
    // literal-built, returned: the control that always survived
    mode harmonic() -> Mx {
        let out = Mx { };
        out.push(4.5);
        return out;
    }
}

